---
export const prerender = true;
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>LLM Primer - One Page Guide</title>
    <style>
        * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
        body { font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.3; color: #333; background: #f5f5f5; }
        @page { size: A4; margin: 0.4in; }
        @media print { body { background: white; } }
        .container { background: white; padding: 0.4in; max-width: 8.5in; height: 11in; margin: 0 auto; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.08in; }
        h1 { font-size: 22px; margin-bottom: 0.05in; color: #1a1a1a; }
        .subtitle { font-size: 10px; color: #666; margin-bottom: 0.08in; }
        h2 { font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.03in; color: #222; border-bottom: 2px solid #FF9800; padding-bottom: 0.02in; }
        table { width: 100%; font-size: 9px; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 0.04in 0; }
        th, td { padding: 0.03in 0.04in; border: 1px solid #ddd; text-align: left; }
        th { background: #f5f5f5; font-weight: 600; }
        p { font-size: 10px; margin-bottom: 0.02in; }
        ul { margin-left: 0.1in; font-size: 10px; }
        li { margin-bottom: 0.015in; }
        .grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 0.08in; }
        .section { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 0.08in; background: #fafafa; }
        .footer { font-size: 8px; color: #999; text-align: center; margin-top: auto; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="container">
        <div>
            <h1>LLM Primer</h1>
            <div class="subtitle">What is an LLM? (one sentence)</div>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <h2>Definition</h2>
            <p>An <strong>LLM (Large Language Model)</strong> is software that predicts the next word by learning patterns from billions of examples.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <h2>Key Terms</h2>
            <table>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Token</strong></td>
                    <td>A piece of text (word, punctuation, subword)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Parameter</strong></td>
                    <td>A "dial" the model uses to predict. More = more nuance.</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Context</strong></td>
                    <td>The conversation history the model can see (4K–400K tokens)</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Hallucination</strong></td>
                    <td>When a model generates plausible-sounding but false info</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
        </div>

        <div class="grid">
            <div class="section">
                <h2>What They Do Well</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Write essays, emails, code</li>
                    <li>Answer questions</li>
                    <li>Explain concepts</li>
                    <li>Summarize documents</li>
                    <li>Brainstorm ideas</li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="section">
                <h2>What They Can't Do</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li>Access the internet</li>
                    <li>Know events after training date</li>
                    <li>Do complex math reliably</li>
                    <li>Guarantee truthfulness</li>
                    <li>Understand beyond ~200K tokens</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="section">
            <h2>3 Ways to Adapt Models</h2>
            <table>
                <tr>
                    <th style="width: 25%;">Method</th>
                    <th>Time</th>
                    <th>Cost</th>
                    <th>When to use</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Prompting</strong></td>
                    <td>Instant</td>
                    <td>Free</td>
                    <td>Writing, analysis, coding</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>RAG</strong></td>
                    <td>Hours</td>
                    <td>Cheap</td>
                    <td>Your own data/docs</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td><strong>Fine-tuning</strong></td>
                    <td>Days</td>
                    <td>Moderate</td>
                    <td>Specific domain/style</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
        </div>

        <div class="footer">AI Playbook Cheat Sheet | May 2026 | Print-friendly, one page</div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
